{"chunk_id": "312aa7fcf937", "text": "Gandhari pleads with her son Duryodhana to abandon his hostility toward the Pandavas and make peace. She argues that true kingship requires self\u2011control, wisdom, and restraint over destructive passions such as lust, wrath, pride, and greed. A ruler who cannot master himself cannot rule others, she warns, and conflict with the virtuous and disciplined Pandavas will only destroy the Kuru house. Gandhari reminds him that Krishna and Arjuna are invincible and urges him to return the Pandavas\u2019 rightful share of the kingdom, noting that half the earth would still provide ample prosperity. Duryodhana ignores her grave counsel and instead conspires with Karna, Shakuni, and Dussasana to capture Krishna during his embassy. Satyaki perceives the plot and quickly prepares a defensive response, foreshadowing escalating crisis.\nGandhari urges Duryodhana to make peace and master his passions, but he rejects her counsel and plots with allies to capture Krishna.\nThemes: maternal counsel, uncontrolled ambition, self-mastery and kingship, ignored warnings, plot against Krishna", "vector": [0.00040791876381263137, -0.007213192526251078, -0.01104415487498045, 0.0002033314958680421, -0.006891713477671146, 0.023133117705583572, -0.0007254214724525809, -0.006064573768526316, -0.028638450428843498, -0.029495729133486748, 0.024151135236024857, 0.005930623970925808, 0.03782740235328674, 0.024740513414144516, -0.015538168139755726, 0.0002668529632501304, 0.05454432964324951, -0.013696359470486641, 0.030647696927189827, -0.021686460822820663, -0.0026086708530783653, -0.004420340992510319, 0.0051637617871165276, 0.007353839930146933, -0.015350638888776302, 0.03142460435628891, 0.007474394515156746, -0.022262444719672203, -0.002568485913798213, -0.021418560296297073, -0.02007906325161457, 0.006185128353536129, 0.03273731470108032, -0.008820589631795883, -0.016649950295686722, 0.011010667309165001, 0.0006948641967028379, -0.00835846271365881, 0.005